ONE LINE: windows is forms in a real Apple window: a click from a point, a resize that relays out, and the behaviours
that wait for both (describe, an image's actions, text editing). Today forms draw to a bitmap or a PDF and a click is mocked.

/*****************************************************************************
    Description
*****************************************************************************/
The line between forms and windows is the window: forms owns attributes, layout, the draw walk and the mock click (click);
windows owns where a click and a size come from, and what a window must keep alive.
Gathered here 2026-11-19 from Topics/forms, Topics/drawing, docs/gcRecon.md and git; each source keeps a one-line pointer.

