    THE CLICK (Tony, 2026-11-04) a click selects the field first, then fires its own action, then its attribute actions left to
                                right. Click actions use onClick:=. Bubbling stays: a member's parent is its enclosing field (built,
                                merge 24beb5f0). Layout's mouseUp calls a kant extern; firing is proved with a synthetic point and
                                no window. (Topics/forms, Events, moved here.)
    THE RESIZE (2026-11-06, 2026-11-10; G3 item 2, 2026-11-21)
                                a resize re-runs setFrame on a fresh deep copy at the frame given (percent stays, SEQ 622 R0). Since G3
                                (SEQ 730) frames are kept by form name in formFrames, for one run: redrawWindow keeps the window's frame,
                                then redraws (a resize, a click redraw); keepFrame alone is a close; setFrame reads and clears the entry
                                for a request naming no frame. layoutFrame and its listener are retired. The window holds its own frame;
                                utilities does not track open windows -- that is this topic's (Tony, 2026-11-21 R3). WAITING: a real
                                window's resize and close calling redrawWindow and keepFrame (frameStoreT, resizeT, resizeLightT).
    DESCRIBE (2026-11-07)       describe's action is a windows behaviour: selecting a field shows its dESCRIPTIONs entry in
                                describeHelp. Today descriptions is layout only; "the describe action and the images' click actions
                                wait for windows" (IncantForms/Windows/descriptions, below its bail). describeAny (same file) is for
                                an inspector in its own window. Seal 441: "the click (select a picture, its text shows in
                                describeHelp) needs a selection and windows, step 10 -- not small." (Topics/forms, Issues, moved here.)
    IMAGES                      images wait for windows: zoom, shrink and centre on the click point come with the click
                                (Topics/drawing, the floor census, image placements; Topics/forms step 10: "images' zoom and field actions come with it").
    THE STAND-IN                the mock click: click(request), a named field, not a point (G1, seal 477; clickT). clickShow(request)
                                (SEQ 737) is click then showForm, for forms that do not redraw by listening (docs/tabsRecon.md, item 4a; tabs
                                stroke 4). Still open from G1: bubbling to the enclosing fields, naming each action skipped, a real
                                point and a window.
    TEXT EDITING (Tony, 2026-11-09, SEQ 585 R2; recorded, not ruled for build)
                                move start to cursor: the field's displayed text (possibly part of a larger text source) restarts at
                                the beginning of the word the cursor is in, or the next word if the cursor is between words, then
                                redisplays. Move end to cursor: the mirror. Try it and adjust. Editing commands are reached by a
                                short selection pop-up rather than memorised keys; a pop-up is itself a form (select a command, its
                                action fires). (git 151b899e; trimmed from Topics/forms since.)
    THE COLLECTOR (measured 2026-11-22, SEQ 747, stroke 0; bought)
                                an open window does NOT hide our globals from the collector. openWindow's GC_set_no_dls(1) stops libgc
                                registering images loaded from then on (197 load at the open) and keeps the roots it has, ours among
                                them. F-153 said the opposite from a comment that was read and never run; closed as not a defect. The
                                witness is windowRootProbe (formsPop windowGcT), with a control that drops every root. Still by hand:
                                the form is held in an uncollectable cell, because a Layout is malloc memory and never scanned -- and
                                once the window holds the laid-out copy, that cell is rewritten at every redraw (stroke 1).

